{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "במדבר סיני", :translit "b'midbar sinai", :gloss "in the wilderness of Sinai"} {:he "אלה המצות", :translit "eleh ha-mitzvot", :gloss "these are the commandments"} {:he "במדבר", :translit "b'midbar", :gloss "in the wilderness"} {:he "אם אין אדם משים עצמו כמדבר אינו יכול לידע תורה ומצות", :translit "im ein adam mashim atzmo k'midbar eino yachol leida torah u-mitzvot", :gloss "if a person does not make himself like a wilderness he cannot know Torah and commandments"} {:he "וכל מעשר בקר וצאן", :translit "v'chol ma'asar bakar v'tzon", :gloss "and every tithe of herd and flock"} {:he "שאו את ראש", :translit "se'u et rosh", :gloss "lift the head [take a count of]"} {:he "עוד תעבורנה הצאן", :translit "od ta'avorneh ha-tzon", :gloss "the flock shall yet pass under the rod"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Semikhah ha-parashiyyot (adjacency of passages): Lev 27:34 'these are the commandments' followed by Num 1:1 'in the wilderness'"} {:kind :other, :note "Semikhah ha-parashiyyot: Lev 27:32 'every tithe of herd and flock' followed by Num 1:2 'lift the head [count]'"} {:kind :other, :note "Resemblance of תעבורנה / תעבירנה (pass under) in Lev 27:32 to תעבורנה in Ezek 20:37, linking counting to passing under the rod"}], :frame {:text "The principle that Torah acquisition requires making oneself hefker like a wilderness appears in Bamidbar Rabbah 1:7, applied to the adjacency of 'these are the commandments' (Lev 27:34) and 'in the wilderness' (Num 1:1). Ezekiel 20:37 states 'I will cause you to pass under the rod' in the context of the wilderness, understood as counting the flock by having them pass one by one. Leviticus 27:32–34 records the tithe of herd and flock passing under the rod, immediately followed by 'these are the commandments.'", :sources ["Bamidbar Rabbah 1:7" "Leviticus 27:32" "Leviticus 27:34" "Ezekiel 20:37"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Semikhah ha-parashiyyot (adjacency of passages): Lev 27:34 '